Third-party material bundled with guildhall.

Kept out of LICENSE on purpose: GitHub identifies a license by matching the file
against known texts, and anything appended after the MIT body makes it
unrecognisable — the repository then reports NOASSERTION and reads as unlicensed,
which for a program that watches your sessions is exactly the wrong first
impression.
Character sprites in assets/characters/ are from pixel-agents
(https://github.com/pixel-agents-hq/pixel-agents), used under the MIT License.
Its notice is preserved in assets/characters/LICENSE-pixel-agents.txt.

The harness marks in src/logos.ts are pixel-art reductions of the Anthropic and
OpenAI logos, drawn for this project rather than copied — no vendor artwork is
redistributed here. They identify which agent a session belongs to, which is what
those marks are for. guildhall is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by
Anthropic or OpenAI, and their trademarks remain their own.

At eleven pixels across a mark cannot be faithful, and brand guidelines generally
ask that logos not be altered. Anyone redistributing or rebranding this should treat
those two sprites as the part to review.
